# Zoho CRM API — local secrets (DO NOT COMMIT the real .env)
# See https://www.zoho.com/crm/developer/docs/api/v2/ (and your data-center docs)

# Accounts OAuth host (must match where you log in)
# ZOHO_ACCOUNTS_URL=https://accounts.zoho.com
# EU: https://accounts.zoho.eu  IN: https://accounts.zoho.in  etc.

# ZOHO_DATA_CENTER=COM
# For EU use EU, IN use IN, etc. — follow Zoho’s API base URL for your org.

# OAuth client (from Zoho API Console → Self Client → Client Secret tab)
#
# OAuth scopes (comma-separated in API Console → Generate Code). Scopes are fixed per refresh token.
#
# Recommended minimum for this repo’s provision/sync scripts + doctor:
#   ZohoCRM.modules.ALL,ZohoCRM.settings.ALL,ZohoCRM.users.ALL,ZohoCRM.apis.READ
# Optional: `provision_quote_client_script.py` (GET/PUT /settings/client_scripts/Quotes) may require a
# separate sub-scope, e.g. ZohoCRM.settings.client_scripts.ALL — pick it in API Console if GET returns 401.
#
# Maximum CRM API v8 breadth (COQL, bulk, org, notifications, API index) — use if you want
# “everything the REST API can do” from one token. Trim if your org policy requires least privilege.
# Docs: https://www.zoho.com/crm/developer/docs/api/v8/scopes.html
#   ZohoCRM.modules.ALL,ZohoCRM.settings.ALL,ZohoCRM.users.ALL,ZohoCRM.org.ALL,ZohoCRM.apis.READ,ZohoCRM.coql.READ,ZohoCRM.bulk.ALL,ZohoCRM.notifications.READ,ZohoCRM.notifications.CREATE,ZohoCRM.notifications.UPDATE,ZohoCRM.notifications.DELETE
#
# Then re-run connect_zoho.py to replace ZOHO_REFRESH_TOKEN after any scope change.
# Run: ./venv/bin/python zoho_doctor.py  — to verify which endpoints your token can hit.
# For API scripts that change settings (e.g. provision_pipelines.py), the grant must include
# ZohoCRM.settings.ALL (or granular settings.* scopes). Modules-only tokens cannot create pipelines.
# provision_phase2_layouts.py needs layouts + map_dependency update scopes (or settings.ALL).
# provision_quoted_line_machine_sku_workflow.py needs workflow + automation (or settings.ALL).
# ZOHO_CLIENT_ID=
# ZOHO_CLIENT_SECRET=

# One-time only: paste grant code from Generate Code, run ./venv/bin/python exchange_grant.py, then remove this line
# ZOHO_GRANT_CODE=

# Self Client token exchange (if https://localhost fails, Zoho may need http://localhost)
# ZOHO_REDIRECT_URI=https://localhost

# After exchange_grant.py: long-lived — treat like a password
# ZOHO_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Optional: from token JSON (ping can also read it from refresh response)
# ZOHO_API_DOMAIN=https://www.zohoapis.com

# Optional: fixed org identifier if your scripts need it
# ZOHO_ORG_ID=

# Optional: Zoho user id for provision_teamspace.py admin when /users?type=CurrentUser is unavailable
# ZOHO_TEAMSPACE_ADMIN_ID=

# Power Query / other tools should read the same names only if you standardize; keep PBI creds in Key Vault/CI, not in git.
